# The credential cache, stated rather than inherited: one record per terminal, so a touch in one terminal never
# authorizes another, and fifteen minutes long, so a dot sync, the dot apply after it and an edit-sync loop in one
# pane ask once. Never global: that hands root to every process of the user, the agents' shells too. A process without
# a terminal falls back to its parent's record, and pam.d/sudo (base/pam) refuses to authenticate it, so it never gets
# one. use_pty keeps a root command off the caller's terminal.
Defaults timestamp_type=tty
Defaults timestamp_timeout=15
Defaults use_pty
